      "writtenOn": "2023-01-05T04:00:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This test doesn\u0027t seem correct. Scenario :\n• There is a regular wifi (100) and an enterprise network (101)\n• wifi disconnects\n\nHere, you don\u0027t update the profile allowed networks. That means you\u0027re not going to clean up the preferences for network 100.\n\nGranted : this is inconsequential unless the netIds rotate after 65k+ connections, and it\u0027s very likely some other event will cleanup soon anyway. However, I think we should have one of two policies :\n❶ Always clean up\n  ... in which case we should just remove this test and always update the allowed networks\n❷ Exploit the fact that it\u0027s inconsequential\n  ...and in that case remove this code and replace with a comment",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4371,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 4371,
        "endChar": 76
      },
